diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index e8498f58a..c8c83c4f2 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -17,13 +17,14 @@ and this project adheres to [Pragmatic Versioning](https://github.com/experiment
 - Single-objective benchmark functions used in the stopping-criteria literature.
 - Any input feature can carry a `Descriptors` block — numeric `columns` and/or a SMILES `structure` column — via `descriptors=Descriptors(...)`. This includes `DiscreteInput`, which had no descriptor support before, and allows a single categorical to carry handcrafted columns *and* structures at once, which the previous class hierarchy could not express.
 - Categorical encodings are first-class data models (`OneHotEncoding`, `OrdinalEncoding`, `DescriptorEncoding`), chosen per surrogate via `categorical_encodings` and extensible like kernels or priors.
-- Data model fields are documented in `Field(description=...)`, so the prose now reaches `model_json_schema()` where users and LLM agents configuring BoFire can read it. `tests/bofire/data_models/test_documentation.py` enforces a description on every field and a docstring on every class, with an allowlist of the models that predate the convention that may only shrink. Migrated so far: acquisition functions, constraints, features, kernels, likelihoods, means, objectives and priors, plus the GP surrogates, the random forest, the MLP ensembles and the surrogate base classes; the remaining packages follow.
+- Data model fields are documented in `Field(description=...)`, so the prose now reaches `model_json_schema()` where users and LLM agents configuring BoFire can read it. `tests/bofire/data_models/test_documentation.py` enforces a description on every field and a docstring on every class, with an allowlist of the models that predate the convention that may only shrink. Migrated so far: acquisition functions, base, constraints, data frames, descriptor generators, domain, encodings, features, kernels, likelihoods, LLM providers, means, objectives, priors and transforms, plus the GP surrogates, the random forest, the MLP ensembles and the surrogate base classes; the remaining packages follow.
 - SHAP feature importance supports categorical outputs by explaining every category probability, including multiclass and mixed continuous/categorical output predictors.
 
 ### Deprecated
 - The non-log acquisition functions `qEI`, `qNEI`, `qEHVI` and `qNEHVI` now emit a `DeprecationWarning` on construction and will be removed in a future release. Use `qLogEI`, `qLogNEI`, `qLogEHVI` and `qLogNEHVI` instead: they optimize the same quantity in log space, which keeps a usable gradient where the plain formulations underflow to zero.
 
 ### Changed
+- **Breaking**: `DropDataTransform.to_be_removed_experiments` and `to_be_removed_candidates` are lists that default to `[]` instead of optional lists defaulting to None; both meant "drop nothing". Serialized transforms with an explicit `null` no longer load. `Fingerprints.bond_radius` and `n_bits` must be positive.
 - **Breaking**: `final_activation` is removed from `RegressionMLPEnsemble` and `ClassificationMLPEnsemble`. Each class allowed a single value, and the networks never read the field. Serialized MLP ensembles carrying it no longer load. `hidden_layer_sizes` must be positive integers, and `dropout` must be below 1. The MLP ensembles now standardize their inputs by default (`scaler=Standardize()` instead of None) and apply a weight decay of 1e-4 (instead of 0), so fitted models change.
 - **Breaking**: `RandomForestSurrogate.oob_score` is removed. It made scikit-learn compute an out-of-bag score that BoFire never used, which only cost fit time. Serialized random forests carrying the field no longer load. `max_features` no longer accepts `"auto"`, which scikit-learn removed in version 1.3: such specs validated but failed when fitting. Its hyperparameters are now bounded (e.g. `n_estimators` and `max_depth` positive, `min_weight_fraction_leaf` in [0, 0.5]), so invalid values are rejected when the spec is built.
 - **Breaking**: `MultiTaskGPSurrogate` is built from components like `SingleTaskGPSurrogate`. Its `noise_prior` and `noise_constraint` move to `likelihood`, and `task_prior` is removed: it was never applied (the fit only warned) and mutated the data model. Serialized multi-task surrogates carrying these fields no longer load. Migrate `MultiTaskGPSurrogate(noise_prior=p, noise_constraint=c)` to `MultiTaskGPSurrogate(likelihood=GaussianLikelihood(noise_prior=p, noise_constraint=c))` to keep one noise level for all tasks as before, or to `likelihood=TaskwiseLikelihood(likelihood=GaussianLikelihood(...))` for one per task. The model now follows BoTorch's default `MultiTaskGP`:
@@ -88,6 +89,7 @@ and this project adheres to [Pragmatic Versioning](https://github.com/experiment
 - LLM field descriptions report descriptor data uniformly for every feature type: a prefix stating what the feature is and its range or options, then the data — `Categorical, allowed: [...] — descriptors per category: {...} — structure: [...]`, `Continuous, bounds [...] — descriptors: {...} — structure: CCO`. Previously the kind was announced in the prefix (`Categorical with descriptors`, `Continuous molecular (SMILES: CCO)`) and only the two descriptor-carrying classes emitted anything.
 
 ### Fixed
+- Clearer validation messages: a data frame with inconsistent continuous output keys no longer reports them as input keys, and unknown `Fragments`/`MordredDescriptors` names are listed instead of the garbled "Not all provided … were not found".
 - `NChooseKConstraint` residual evaluation ignores unrelated experiment metadata and preserves row labels, avoiding object-dtype errors and misalignment when combined with other constraints. ([#855](https://github.com/experimental-design/bofire/issues/855))
 - `QparegoStrategy` draws independent Chebyshev scalarization weights for each candidate in a batch, instead of reusing one trade-off direction for the whole batch (#849). Baseline predictions and output constraints are shared across candidates.
 - Sigmoid and target-window objectives use stable sigmoid evaluations, preventing NaN acquisition gradients in saturated regions and preserving small rewards in decreasing tails. ([#853](https://github.com/experimental-design/bofire/issues/853))
